{
  "title": "The middle and passive voice",
  "note": "In the middle voice the subject acts on or for itself; in the passive it receives the action. In the present they share one set of forms: λύομαι, λύῃ, λύεται, λυόμεθα, λύεσθε, λύονται, 'I am loosed' (or 'I loose for myself'). The agent of a passive is ὑπό + genitive. Deponent verbs have middle forms but active meanings: ἔρχομαι, I come.",
